-> Reference: handlers — `ClassName => { body }` defines a handler; the
-> particle's fields are in scope by name inside the body. `emit <particle>
-> to <target> get <result>` dispatches — targets are `this` (current
-> module), `base` (the module that linked this one), `core` (built-in
-> handlers), or a linked module's alias.
Ping = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Ping", value ∈ Number }
Pong = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Pong", value ∈ Number }

Ping => {
    return Pong { value = value + 1 }
}

emit Ping { value = 10 } to this get result
assert result.value = 11
